ion that reported on the restrictions and their impact during the third wave of the pandemic in Poland,1\r\n466,WOSZCZYŃSKI,Author mentioned in the context of innovative and secure banking practices,1\r\n65,SWATCHPAY,\"SwatchPay is a mobile payment system launched in December 2020, designed for use with Swatch watches\",1\r\n114,PLUS BANK,\"PLUS BANK is a financial institution based in Poland. It provides its customers with the convenience of using Google Pay, a popular digital wallet platform that allows users to make payments using their smartphones. However, PLUS BANK does not currently support the BLIK payment system, which is another widely used mobile payment method in Poland. Despite this limitation, PLUS BANK continues to serve its clients by offering a range of banking services and digital payment solutions, including the integration with Google Pay, to enhance the banking experience for its customers.\",2\r\n39,MBANK,\"mBank is a prominent financial institution in Poland, recognized as a leader in mobile banking services. Established as a pioneer in the field, mBank introduced WAP-based mobile banking as early as 2000, marking its commitment to technological advancement. The bank has played a significant role in the development of mobile banking and the Polish Standard of Payments, contributing to the creation of the BLIK payment system alongside five other banks. Since 2015, mBank has been offering BLIK services to its customers, further solidifying its position in the mobile payment landscape.\n\nmBank provides a comprehensive suite of mobile banking services, catering to a large user base that includes 2.59 million active mobile app users and 3.95 million individual clients. The bank's mobile application is frequently analyzed for its usage metrics, reflecting its importance in the digital banking sector. mBank offers a variety of mobile payment systems, including BLIK, Google Pay, Apple Pay, Garmin Pay, Fitbit Pay, Swatch PAY!, and Xiaomi Pay, ensuring